Event the First: A monster zapped a digging wand on the up stairs,
leaving me no way to escape the Mines. (This was a very young game.) I
had never encountered this before. I had never even considered this
before. So I guess I have a new rule: Don't fight monsters that are
camped on the up stairs unless I know they can't dig or I don't care if
they dig.

Event the Second: On turn 2, my kitten falls into a pit, but I don't
recognize this. On turn 4, I move to where the kitten is, thinking I'll
just displace her; actually, I fall into her pit while she gets
frightened and goes feral. On turn 6, while I try to exit the pit, she
bites me to death.

